        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9e2a0ba1-51b2-5036-9426-7b897a31b594",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elizabeth Smylie, Vasek Pospisil, Jack Sock, Bobby Reynolds, Nicole Provis, Jo-Anne Faull, Julie Richardson, Pierre-Ludovic Duclos, Ivo Klec\n- Events: Wimbledon Championships, Indian Wells Masters, Dow Classic, Jalisco Open\n- Topics: professional tennis, Grand Slam titles, doubles, mixed doubles\n\nFacts:\n- Elizabeth Smylie, née Sayers and sometimes known as Liz Smylie, was born on 11 April 1963 and is a retired Australian professional tennis player.\n- Elizabeth Smylie won four Grand Slam titles during her career, including one in women's doubles and three in mixed doubles.\n- Vasek Pospisil and Bobby Reynolds won the first edition of the 2011 Jalisco Open doubles event by defeating Pierre-Ludovic Duclos and Ivo Klec 6–4, 6–7(6), [10–6] in the final.\n- Nicole Provis and Elizabeth Smylie entered the 1992 Dow Classic doubles event as defending champions, but Jo-Anne Faull and Julie Richardson defeated them in the quarterfinals.\n- Vasek Pospisil and Jack Sock won the 2014 Wimbledon Championships men's doubles title and the 2015 Indian Wells Masters men's doubles title.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "42010621-77e6-5687-bbc9-8ce2027895b5",
        "text": "Page: Elizabeth Smylie. Sentence: Elizabeth Smylie (née Sayers, born 11 April 1963), sometimes known as Liz Smylie, is a retired Australian professional tennis player.\nPage: Elizabeth Smylie. Sentence: During her career, she won four Grand Slam titles, one of them in women's doubles and three in mixed doubles.\nPage: Vasek Pospisil. Sentence: Along with partner Jack Sock, he won the 2014 Wimbledon Championships and the 2015 Indian Wells Masters men's doubles titles.\nPage: 1992 Dow Classic – Doubles. Sentence: Nicole Provis and Elizabeth Smylie were the defending champions but were defeated in the quarterfinals by Jo-Anne Faull and Julie Richardson.\nPage: 2011 Jalisco Open – Doubles. Sentence: Vasek Pospisil and Bobby Reynolds won the first edition of this tournament, beating Pierre-Ludovic Duclos and Ivo Klec 6–4, 6–7(6), [10–6] in the final.",
